h with InStr what you want and number how many characters you have to skip to find the version."},{"owner":{"account_id":3024623,"reputation":434,"user_id":2564908,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":0,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/kWljr.png?s=256","display_name":"David Egan","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/2564908/david-egan"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":2176787,"reputation":198,"user_id":1927287,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/91ac9903697ec82de0aad08c10badf4c?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"ferdo","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/1927287/ferdo"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1500900608,"post_id":45237882,"comment_id":77524525,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","body":"I need to be able to establish the LastSaveVersion by programming means. Ideally C#. Been able to see this information in a text editor is really no good to me. it hast to be by programmatic means."},{"owner":{"account_id":2176787,"reputation":198,"user_id":1927287,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/91ac9903697ec82de0aad08c10badf4c?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"ferdo","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/1927287/ferdo"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1500824086,"post_id":45237882,"comment_id":77496445,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","body":"You can find LASTSaveVersion by simply opening your CATIA files in an text editor and search the string you mentioned. Look at the files in text editor, you can find also service pack, hot fix, FirstStreamed for V6 files and many other things..."}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":149}